gn give him upside if the fall environment breaks his way"], "rationale": "South Carolina's Republican lean, Wilson's statewide profile, and two summer polls showing an eight-point Republican lead all point the same direction, with markets pricing a Democratic win at just five to six percent. Johnson's primary upset makes him a credible nominee but not yet a competitive one in this environment.", "watch": "A sharply favorable national environment for Democrats, a standout performance in the three scheduled debates, or fresh fall polling moving toward Johnson could narrow the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Henry McMaster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's governorship is open this year as Henry McMaster terms out, and Republicans have turned to Attorney General Alan Wilson, a well-known statewide official. Democrats nominated state Representative Jermaine Johnson, who surprised observers by winning his primary and has campaigned actively with a running mate, a faith tour, and a series of scheduled debates.\n\nThe race still leans firmly Republican. Two Democratic-sponsored polls from July and August showed Wilson ahead by eight points, and prediction markets give Johnson only about a five to six percent chance. National race raters uniformly place the contest in the Solid or Likely Republican column. South Carolina's Republican lean at the presidential level frames the contest, and the open seat does not change the state's fundamentals. Johnson needs a sharply favorable fall environment or a debate breakthrough to become competitive; current evidence points to a comfortable Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0588, "margin": -9.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0722, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0597, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0544, "margin": -9.5}]}